('127.110.d.11.I',3,'A control circuit can be tested by checking for voltage across the:','["Coil when the start button is pressed", "Wall", "Floor", "Window"]'::jsonb,0,'Coil voltage proves control.','original'),
('127.110.d.11.I',4,'A coil that does not pull in when voltage is present is probably:','["Overfilled", "Defective", "Working normally", "Painted"]'::jsonb,1,'Replace the coil.','original'),
('127.110.d.12.A',3,'Light enters the eye through the:','["Heel", "Knee", "Pupil", "Lens cap"]'::jsonb,2,'The pupil admits light.','original'),
('127.110.d.12.A',4,'The part of the eye that senses light and sends signals to the brain is the:','["Cornea only", "Iris", "Eyelid", "Retina"]'::jsonb,3,'Retina has rods and cones.','original'),
('127.110.d.12.B',3,'Light is a form of:','["Electromagnetic energy", "Chemical fuel", "Sound energy", "Heat only"]'::jsonb,0,'Visible radiation.','original'),
('127.110.d.12.B',4,'The unit used to measure illumination on a surface is the:','["Ampere", "Footcandle", "Hertz", "Ohm"]'::jsonb,1,'Footcandles measure light level.','original'),
('127.110.d.12.C',3,'LED lamps are known for their:','["High heat", "High cost of power", "Long life and efficiency", "Short life"]'::jsonb,2,'LEDs are efficient.','original'),
('127.110.d.12.C',4,'Compared with incandescent lamps, fluorescent lamps are more:','["Short-lived", "Heat-producing", "Silent without parts", "Efficient, but need a ballast"]'::jsonb,3,'Ballasts regulate current.','original'),
('127.110.d.12.D',3,'When replacing a lamp, always check that the new lamp has the correct:','["Wattage and base type", "Brand of tape", "Name", "Color of the box"]'::jsonb,0,'Match ratings.','original'),
('127.110.d.12.D',4,'Before changing a lamp in a fixture, the circuit should be:','["Painted", "Turned off", "Left on", "Overloaded"]'::jsonb,1,'Safety first.','original'),
('127.110.d.12.E',3,'Recessed lighting fixtures are installed:','["Under the floor", "On top of the roof", "Into the ceiling so the housing is hidden", "On the street"]'::jsonb,2,'Recessed are flush.','original'),
('127.110.d.12.E',4,'A fixture marked IC may be installed:','["Only in the open", "Where insulation is not allowed", "Under water", "In direct contact with insulation"]'::jsonb,3,'Insulation contact rated.','original'),
('127.111.d.1.A',3,'The basic purpose of an HVAC system is to control indoor:','["Temperature, humidity, and air quality", "Wall color", "Furniture style", "Floor texture"]'::jsonb,0,'HVAC conditions air.','original'),
('127.111.d.1.A',4,'The three basic HVAC functions are heating, cooling, and:','["Painting", "Ventilation", "Sanding", "Plumbing"]'::jsonb,1,'Ventilation refreshes air.','original'),
('127.111.d.1.B',3,'The Clean Air Act affects HVAC technicians because it limits:','["Thermostat styles", "Duct shapes", "The release of refrigerants", "Paint colors"]'::jsonb,2,'Refrigerants harm ozone.','original'),
('127.111.d.1.B',4,'Technicians who handle refrigerants must be:','["Unlicensed", "Under age", "Unpaid", "Certified under EPA rules"]'::jsonb,3,'EPA 608 certification.','original'),
('127.111.d.1.C',3,'A drawing that shows duct sizes and layout is a:','["Mechanical plan", "Menu", "Landscape plan", "Poster"]'::jsonb,0,'Mechanical plans show HVAC.','original'),
