('127.111.d.2.A',4,'A pound in the English system corresponds to what unit in the SI system for mass?','["Joule", "Meter", "Liter", "Kilogram"]'::jsonb,3,'Mass uses kg.','original'),
('127.111.d.2.B',3,'To convert 12,000 BTU per hour into tons of cooling, divide by:','["12,000", "120", "24", "1,200,000"]'::jsonb,0,'One ton equals 12,000 BTU/h.','original'),
('127.111.d.2.B',4,'A room measures 10 ft by 12 ft by 8 ft. Its volume is:','["96 cubic feet", "960 cubic feet", "120 cubic feet", "30 cubic feet"]'::jsonb,1,'10 x 12 x 8 = 960.','original'),
('127.111.d.2.C',3,'Water freezes at 0 degrees Celsius, which is how many degrees Fahrenheit?','["100", "0", "32", "212"]'::jsonb,2,'Freezing is 32 F.','original'),
('127.111.d.2.C',4,'A temperature of 68 degrees Fahrenheit is how many degrees Celsius?','["40", "36", "68", "20"]'::jsonb,3,'(68-32) x 5/9 = 20.','original'),
('127.111.d.3.A',3,'When installing refrigerant piping, the lines should be kept:','["Clean and dry inside", "Dirty", "Open to the air", "Wet"]'::jsonb,0,'Contamination damages systems.','original'),
('127.111.d.3.A',4,'Moisture inside a refrigerant line can cause:','["Extra capacity", "Acid formation and freeze-ups", "Better cooling", "Lower pressure"]'::jsonb,1,'Moisture harms systems.','original'),
('127.111.d.3.B',3,'Copper tubing for refrigerant is cut with a:','["Chisel", "Hacksaw only", "Tubing cutter", "Axe"]'::jsonb,2,'Cutters make square cuts.','original'),
('127.111.d.3.B',4,'Soft copper tubing is bent using a:','["Torch alone", "Hammer", "Vise only", "Tubing bender or spring"]'::jsonb,3,'Benders prevent kinks.','original'),
('127.111.d.3.C',3,'A flare fitting connects tubing by:','["Flaring the tube end against a seat", "Taping", "Welding", "Gluing"]'::jsonb,0,'Flare seals metal-to-metal.','original'),
('127.111.d.3.C',4,'Before flaring a tube, slip the flare nut on:','["Never", "First, over the tube end", "After flaring", "On the compressor"]'::jsonb,1,'Nut must be on first.','original'),
('127.111.d.3.D',3,'Refrigerant pipes are supported with:','["Glue", "Rope", "Hangers or clamps at proper spacing", "Tape"]'::jsonb,2,'Supports prevent sagging.','original'),
('127.111.d.3.D',4,'Refrigerant lines should be supported so vibration does not:','["Add efficiency", "Reduce noise", "Cool the room", "Crack the tubing at fittings"]'::jsonb,3,'Vibration causes leaks.','original'),
('127.111.d.3.E',3,'Piping that carries refrigerant to an outdoor unit is called the:','["Line set", "Gas stove", "Filter", "Drain pan"]'::jsonb,0,'Line sets connect units.','original'),
('127.111.d.3.E',4,'Insulation on the larger suction line prevents:','["Cooling", "Sweating and heat gain", "Pressure drop to zero", "Corrosion of the roof"]'::jsonb,1,'Cold line sweats.','original'),
('127.111.d.3.F',3,'After installation, a refrigerant system is often tested with:','["Air with oil", "Oxygen", "Dry nitrogen under pressure", "Water"]'::jsonb,2,'Nitrogen is safe and dry.','original'),
