('127.111.d.6.F',3,'A filter drier in a refrigeration line removes:','["Moisture and particles", "Voltage", "Sound", "Heat"]'::jsonb,0,'Driers protect the system.','original'),
('127.111.d.6.F',4,'A sight glass on a liquid line lets the technician see:','["The room color", "Whether liquid refrigerant is flowing", "The voltage", "The temperature"]'::jsonb,1,'Bubbles can show low charge.','original'),
('127.111.d.6.G',3,'A thermostat controls a cooling system by:','["Changing the color", "Making noise", "Turning equipment on and off to hold a set temperature", "Moving ducts"]'::jsonb,2,'Thermostats cycle equipment.','original'),
('127.111.d.6.G',4,'A low-pressure switch shuts off the compressor to protect it when pressure is too:','["Hot", "Neutral", "High only", "Low"]'::jsonb,3,'Protects against loss of charge.','original'),
('127.111.d.6.H',3,'Refrigeration piping must be sloped and sized to ensure:','["Oil returns to the compressor", "Noise", "Heat loss", "Water stays out"]'::jsonb,0,'Oil return is critical.','original'),
('127.111.d.6.H',4,'A trap in a vertical suction line helps:','["Create noise", "Carry oil up toward the compressor", "Hold water", "Stop flow"]'::jsonb,1,'Traps aid oil return.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.A',3,'The three methods of heat transfer are conduction, convection, and:','["Ventilation", "Insulation", "Radiation", "Evaporation"]'::jsonb,2,'Radiation is heat by waves.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.A',4,'Feeling heat from the sun on your skin is an example of:','["Condensation", "Conduction", "Convection", "Radiation"]'::jsonb,3,'Solar energy radiates.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.B',3,'Combustion requires fuel, oxygen, and:','["Heat", "Water", "Ice", "Wind alone"]'::jsonb,0,'Fire triangle.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.B',4,'A dangerous by-product of incomplete combustion is:','["Water vapor", "Carbon monoxide", "Oxygen", "Nitrogen"]'::jsonb,1,'CO is toxic.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.C',3,'Fuels used for heating include natural gas, propane, and:','["Air", "Sand", "Fuel oil", "Water"]'::jsonb,2,'Common fuels.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.C',4,'Propane is stored as a liquid under:','["Water", "Vacuum", "Sand", "Pressure in a tank"]'::jsonb,3,'LP is pressurized.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.D',3,'An induced draft furnace uses a fan to:','["Pull flue gases through the heat exchanger", "Pump water", "Fill the tank", "Cool the room"]'::jsonb,0,'Inducer moves gases.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.D',4,'A heat exchanger separates combustion gases from the:','["Gas supply", "Air being delivered to the building", "Thermostat", "Filter"]'::jsonb,1,'Keeps gases out of the house.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.E',3,'When installing a furnace, the installer must provide proper clearances and:','["Ornaments", "Paint", "Venting and combustion air", "Flowers"]'::jsonb,2,'Safe operation.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.E',4,'Clearance to combustibles is listed on the furnace:','["Filter", "Box", "Cover art", "Data plate"]'::jsonb,3,'Follow the label.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.F',3,'In a gas furnace, the gas valve controls the flow of gas to the:','["Burners", "Filter", "Thermostat", "Duct"]'::jsonb,0,'Valve opens on call for heat.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.F',4,'A flame sensor proves to the control that:','["The room is cool", "The burners have lit", "The filter is clean", "The duct is open"]'::jsonb,1,'Prevents gas flow without flame.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.G',3,'A manometer is used to measure:','["Humidity", "Voltage", "Gas pressure", "Weight"]'::jsonb,2,'Manometers read low pressures.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.G',4,'Natural gas manifold pressure is commonly set near how many inches of water column?','["0.35", "35", "350", "3.5"]'::jsonb,3,'Typical NG manifold is 3.5 in. w.c.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.H',3,'An oil furnace burns fuel oil sprayed through a:','["Nozzle", "Filter only", "Duct", "Coil"]'::jsonb,0,'Atomizing nozzle.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.H',4,'The oil burner ignites the spray with a:','["Lighter", "Spark from electrodes", "Match", "Candle"]'::jsonb,1,'Electrodes ignite oil.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.I',3,'Preventive furnace maintenance includes replacing the:','["Floor", "Windows", "Air filter", "Roof"]'::jsonb,2,'Dirty filters hurt flow.','original'),
('127.111.d.7.I',4,'Cleaning burners and checking the flue helps ensure:','["Lower safety", "Poor draft", "Higher noise", "Safe, efficient combustion"]'::jsonb,3,'Regular maintenance.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.A',3,'In a forced-air system, a blower moves air through:','["Supply and return ducts", "Electric wire", "Gas lines", "Water pipes"]'::jsonb,0,'Ducts carry air.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.A',4,'Air pressure in the supply duct is generally:','["Random", "Positive compared with the room", "Negative", "Zero"]'::jsonb,1,'Supply is pressurized.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.B',3,'A centrifugal fan moves air by:','["Heating it", "Pushing straight with a prop", "Throwing it outward from a rotating wheel", "Burning it"]'::jsonb,2,'Centrifugal action.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.B',4,'A propeller fan is best for moving:','["Water", "Air through long ducts", "Gas", "Large volumes at low pressure"]'::jsonb,3,'Propeller fans are low pressure.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.C',3,'A duct system that branches from a main trunk is a:','["Trunk-and-branch system", "Radiator", "Boiler", "Tank"]'::jsonb,0,'Common design.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.C',4,'Flexible duct is useful for:','["Fuel lines", "Short connections to registers", "Flue gas", "Underground mains"]'::jsonb,1,'Flex is easy to route.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.D',3,'Metal duct sections are joined with seams and then sealed with:','["Water", "Wax", "Mastic or approved tape", "Paper"]'::jsonb,2,'Sealing prevents leaks.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.D',4,'Fiberboard duct is cut using a:','["Axe", "Hammer", "Torch", "Special knife and straightedge"]'::jsonb,3,'Fiberboard is knife-cut.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.E',3,'A transition in a duct system is used to change:','["Duct size or shape", "Color", "Voltage", "Fuel"]'::jsonb,0,'Transitions adapt ducts.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.E',4,'A smooth transition reduces air:','["Capacity", "Turbulence and pressure loss", "Noise", "Flow rate"]'::jsonb,1,'Gradual changes help.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.F',3,'A diffuser delivers air into a room and:','["Stores water", "Removes air", "Spreads it to avoid drafts", "Heats gas"]'::jsonb,2,'Diffusers distribute.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.F',4,'Return grilles are generally placed where they can:','["Blow air out", "Hold dust", "Heat water", "Draw room air back to the system"]'::jsonb,3,'Returns collect air.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.G',3,'A damper in a duct is used to:','["Regulate or stop air flow", "Heat air", "Filter dust", "Make noise"]'::jsonb,0,'Dampers control airflow.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.G',4,'A fire damper closes automatically when:','["Fan stops", "Heat melts its fusible link", "Lights turn on", "The thermostat is set"]'::jsonb,1,'Prevents fire spread.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.H',3,'Duct insulation helps:','["Block light", "Lower strength", "Reduce heat loss or gain", "Raise noise"]'::jsonb,2,'Insulation saves energy.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.H',4,'A vapor barrier on cold duct insulation prevents:','["Heat flow", "Fire", "Rust of fans", "Condensation on or in the insulation"]'::jsonb,3,'Barriers block moisture.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.I',3,'An anemometer is used to measure:','["Air velocity", "Temperature of metal", "Gas pressure", "Voltage"]'::jsonb,0,'Anemometers measure speed.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.I',4,'A pitot tube with a manometer measures air:','["Humidity", "Velocity pressure in a duct", "Sound", "Weight"]'::jsonb,1,'Used for air balancing.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.J',3,'To find the air volume in a duct, multiply the velocity by the duct''s:','["Weight", "Length", "Cross-sectional area", "Color"]'::jsonb,2,'CFM = velocity x area.','original'),
('127.111.d.8.J',4,'Air moving at 600 feet per minute through a 2-square-foot duct delivers:','["300 cfm", "602 cfm", "12 cfm", "1,200 cubic feet per minute"]'::jsonb,3,'600 x 2 = 1200.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
